<p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/037J">Definition <span data-tag="037J">5.3.5.1</span>.</a> Let $\operatorname{\mathcal{C}}$ be a category and let $\mathscr {F}_0, \mathscr {F}_{1}: \operatorname{\mathcal{C}}\rightarrow \operatorname{QCat}$ be diagrams of $\infty $-categories indexed by $\operatorname{\mathcal{C}}$. We will say that $\mathscr {F}_0$ and $\mathscr {F}_1$ are <em>levelwise equivalent</em> if there exists another diagram $\mathscr {F}: \operatorname{\mathcal{C}}\rightarrow \operatorname{QCat}$ equipped with levelwise categorical equivalences $\mathscr {F}_0 \rightarrow \mathscr {F} \leftarrow \mathscr {F}_1$ (see Definition <a data-tag="0347" href="/tag/0347">4.5.7.1</a>). </p>
</article>
